---
import { homeFaqs, productInfo, siteConfig } from '../data/site';

const shareUrl = encodeURIComponent(siteConfig.url + '/');
const shareText = encodeURIComponent('Overwatch Hacks — undetected ESP & aimbot for PC');
---

<section class="home-seo shell" aria-labelledby="home-seo-title">
	<div class="home-seo__panel card-surface">
		<h2 id="home-seo-title">Overwatch Hacks for Windows PC</h2>
		<p>
			{productInfo.summary} Use this page to compare ESP, aimbot, wallhack, pricing, and where to check
			status after Blizzard anti-cheat patches.
		</p>
		<p>
			Overwatch is a high-information game: control points, flank routes, and team pushes punish guesswork. Overwatch Hacks
			is built for that pressure — readable ESP and aimbot controls on Windows PC, with maintenance notes
			after patches instead of empty “always undetected” claims.
		</p>
		<p>
			Start with the <a href="/overwatch-hacks/">Overwatch Hacks guide</a>, then check
			<a href="/overwatch-esp/">ESP</a>, <a href="/overwatch-aimbot/">Aimbot</a>,
			<a href="/features/">Features</a>, and <a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a>.
			Official client updates ship from
			<a href="https://overwatch.blizzard.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Overwatch</a>;
			anti-cheat context from
			<a href="https://www.easy.ac/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Blizzard anti-cheat</a>.
			Confirm our <a href="/updates/">Updates log</a> before you load in.
		</p>

		<div class="home-seo__grid">
			<article>
				<h3><a href="/overwatch-hacks/">Overwatch Hacks guide</a></h3>
				<p>Pillar overview: ESP, aimbot, wallhack, and how maintenance works after patches.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3><a href="/overwatch-esp/">Overwatch ESP</a></h3>
				<p>Player and loot visibility with distance readouts for control point play.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3><a href="/overwatch-aimbot/">Overwatch Aimbot</a></h3>
				<p>Smoothness, FOV, bone priority, and hotkeys for PC and controllers.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3><a href="/overwatch-wallhack/">Overwatch wallhack</a></h3>
				<p>Wallhack-style overlays for players and containers when ESP categories stay on.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3><a href="/overwatch-hacks/">Undetected status</a></h3>
				<p>How EAC rebuilds ship, what “undetected” means here, and where to check status.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3><a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a></h3>
				<p>Monthly and lifetime licenses with digital delivery after payment confirmation.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3><a href="/setup/">Setup</a></h3>
				<p>Activate the package, tune overlays, and get ready for your first session.</p>
			</article>
			<article>
				<h3><a href="/faq/">FAQ</a></h3>
				<p>Straight answers on delivery, maintenance, platforms, and support.</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="home-seo__panel card-surface">
		<h2>What the package includes</h2>
		<p>
			Sold for Overwatch on Windows PC. ESP covers players, loot, and distance. Aimbot adds assisted targeting
			with smoothness and hotkeys. General options include in-client toggles, monthly and lifetime plans,
			patch notices, and support.
		</p>
		<ul>
			{productInfo.features.esp.slice(0, 3).map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
			{productInfo.features.aimbot.slice(0, 2).map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
			{productInfo.features.general.slice(0, 2).map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
		</ul>
		<p>
			Compare plans on <a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a>. Watch
			<a href="/updates/">Updates</a> after game patches. Policies live in the footer.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="home-seo__panel card-surface">
		<h2>How to evaluate before you buy</h2>
		<p>
			If threat awareness comes first, open the ESP page. If firefights matter more, review Aimbot controls.
			Most buyers check both, then pick monthly or lifetime on Pricing. Platforms today:
			{productInfo.platforms.join(', ')}. Market: {siteConfig.market}.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="home-seo__panel card-surface">
		<h2 id="faq-heading">FAQ</h2>
		<div class="home-seo__faq">
			{homeFaqs.map((item) => (
				<details>
					<summary>{item.question}</summary>
					<p set:html={item.answer} />
				</details>
			))}
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="home-seo__share" aria-label="Share">
		<a
			href={`https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url=${shareUrl}&text=${shareText}`}
			rel="noopener noreferrer"
			target="_blank"
		>
			Share
		</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.home-seo {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		padding-block: var(--section-space);
	}

	.home-seo__panel {
		padding: 1.35rem 1.4rem;
		border-radius: var(--radius-card);
	}

	.home-seo__panel h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 1.65rem);
		font-weight: 750;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}

	.home-seo__panel p,
	.home-seo__panel li {
		color: var(--color-muted);
		line-height: 1.65;
		font-size: 0.98rem;
	}

	.home-seo__panel a {
		color: var(--color-orchid);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
	}

	.home-seo__grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.85rem;
		margin-top: 1.25rem;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
	}

	.home-seo__grid article {
		padding: 0.85rem 0.9rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 0.55rem;
		background: rgba(20, 24, 28, 0.55);
	}

	.home-seo__grid h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.home-seo__grid p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.home-seo__faq details {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		padding: 0.75rem 0;
	}

	.home-seo__faq summary {
		cursor: pointer;
		font-weight: 650;
		color: var(--color-ink);
	}

	.home-seo__faq p {
		margin: 0.55rem 0 0;
	}

	.home-seo__share {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: flex-end;
	}

	.home-seo__share a {
		color: var(--color-faint);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
</style>
